00:01:03,953 --> 00:01:06,989
=Wow The World S2=

10
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:12,560
Water management embodies
Dujiangyan's age-old wisdom.

11
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:15,040
Over two thousand years ago,

12
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:16,720
water from the Min River surged down

13
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:18,120
from Min Mountain on the western edge
of the Chengdu Plain.

14
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:20,680
The fierce, raging currents

15
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:22,480
often caused devastating floods.

16
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,400
That changed when Li Bing, Governor
of Shu Prefecture under the Qin Dynasty,

17
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:26,600
led the local people

18
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:28,800
to build Dujiangyan
at the outlet of the Min River,

19
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:31,800
a remarkable water conservancy project

20
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:32,939
(Magical Dujiangyan)
built without tall dams or sluice gates.

21
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:36,080
Three core structures make up
the entire headworks.

22
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:37,080
(Water-Dividing Dyke)
Fish Mouth

23
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:39,960
is the fish-shaped dividing dike in the middle of the river.

24
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:41,520
(Inner River, Outer River)
It splits Min River into two channels.

25
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:42,840
(Flood Discharge)
The Outer River diverts floodwaters,

26
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:44,520
(Water Diversion for Irrigation)
while the Inner River draws water for irrigation.

27
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:46,080
(Dry Season, 60% Inner River, Fish Mouth, 40% Outer River)
Cleverly utilizing river bends,

28
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:47,837
it channels 60% of clean water
into the Inner River during dry seasons

29
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,480
to secure irrigation supplies. (Flood Season)

30
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:52,058
In flood seasons,
60% of the slit-laden floodwater

31
00:01:52,058 --> 00:01:53,440
(40% Inner River, 60% Outer River)
is flushed into the Outer River

32
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:54,560
to mitigate disasters.

33
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:55,480
This is the ingenious principle

34
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:58,080
known as "Sixty-Forty Division,
Balancing Flood and Drought".

35
00:01:58,343 --> 00:01:59,160
(Feishayan, Outer River,
Inner River, Fish Mouth)

36
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,960
Situated along the bend
of the Inner River is the Feishayan.

37
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:04,200
Its crest stands merely two meters
above the riverbed.

38
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:07,320
When water levels are low, it retains
water and feeds it into the channels.

39
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:10,039
When water rises, floods automatically
overflow to discharge.

40
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:13,080
Meanwhile, the centrifugal force
generated by the river bend

41
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:15,640
(Silt and Stones)
hurls silt and stones into the Outer River,

42
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:17,000
preventing siltation.

43
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:17,600
This embodies the principle of

44
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:19,910
"Deep Dredging of the Shoals,
Low Constructions of the Weirs".

45
00:02:19,910 --> 00:02:21,400
(Feishayan, Fish Mouth) Baopingkou

46
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:23,080
(AI-generated Content)
is a narrow gap

47
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:25,360
chiseled out of rocky mountains over
eight years under Li Bing's leadership.

48
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,120
Narrow as it looks,

49
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:28,200
it acts as the master regulator

50
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:30,600
controlling the water volume flowing
into the Chengdu Plain,

51
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,600
keeping water supply stable
in both drought and flood.

52
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:35,600
This hydraulic project has served
for more than 2,000 years

53
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:37,680
and still functions to this day.

54
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:39,880
It transformed the once disaster-prone
Chengdu Plain

55
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:41,560
into the Land of Abundance.

56
